<http://wittgensteiniana.michelepasin.org/id/topic/logical-space-by-wittgenstein> a schema:DefinedTerm ;
    schema:description "Wittgenstein says that facts (or better, state of affairs) exists in the realm of everything which is logically possible, that is, everything which can be true or false. This 'dimension' is the logical space ." ;
    schema:inDefinedTermSet id:topics ;
    schema:name "Logical Space" .

<http://wittgensteiniana.michelepasin.org/id/topic/mystical-by-wittgenstein> a schema:DefinedTerm ;
    schema:description "The awareness of the ineffability of those things that we feel most compelled to understand is what is mystical." ;
    schema:inDefinedTermSet id:topics ;
    schema:name "Mystical" .

<http://wittgensteiniana.michelepasin.org/id/topic/primitive-sign-by-wittgenstein> a schema:DefinedTerm ;
    schema:description "A primitive sign is a simple symbol - a symbol for names - which cannot be further defined: it is fully analyzed." ;
    schema:inDefinedTermSet id:topics ;
    schema:name "Primitive Sign" .

<http://wittgensteiniana.michelepasin.org/id/topic/thing-by-wittgenstein> a schema:DefinedTerm ;
    schema:description "In the Tractatus, it seems that things are the equivalent of objects - with the difference that the former are usually related to facts, while the latter to state of affairs." ;
